          "UNRESOLVED (p.71): lower lateral double K L13-L13 1/2 and the 33 WF 130 strut at L13 1/2; the inverted portal L13 1/2-L15 (Sheets 44 / 45) - the L13 1/2 point is not dimensioned on the sheets read. not built.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.71): sway bracing above the floor beams and the portal knee bracing - only the V frames below the floor beams are tabulated on p.71. V frames 0-12 built; nothing above the floor beams except the U11 portal strut envelope.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.94, p.86): upper pin of the rope suspenders - p.94 details the socket and the floor beam end only; the suspender support diaphragm at the lower chord is on Sheet 46 (p.86, not read). upper pin 2\u0027-11 1/4 below the CL of the lower chord (half chord depth 1\u0027-5 1/4 \u002B 1\u0027-6 as at the floor beam).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.94): number of ropes per suspender point - View E-E draws one 4\u0022 rope on the CL truss but does not state the count. one rope per point and truss.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.70, p.74-90): rivets - the joint sheets draw the rivets and give their sizes (1 1/4 / 1 1/8 H.S., 1\u0022 stitch, 7/8 floor) but print no counts. rivets are not placed (the program places rivet groups when counts / pitch are given).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.69, p.74-90): chord splice plates, inlay plates, fills, lug angles, stiffeners, diaphragms and stitch rivets - they are listed per joint without their extents. not built (the steel weight check shows what is missing).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.69, p.70): perforated cover plates (manholes 12 x 20 / 11 1/2 x 20 at 3\u0027-6 or 4\u0027-0) - spacing printed as approximate. covers built solid (weight overstated by the manholes).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.69, p.74): order of the web plies of the chords - the sections list the plies without their order; the half section L13-L17 shows inlays at the joints. plies stacked from the outside in the printed order, angles against the innermost ply deeper than their leg.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.73): hold-down rollers and shear lock at piers 17 / 20 - detailed on p.73 but not part of this phase. not built."
        ]
      }
    },
